`verilator_config
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Documented Verilator warning waivers. Policy: no global suppression —
// every entry names the file/pattern, the observed message, and why it is
// benign. Remove an entry and re-lint to re-audit it.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

// [upstream dependency: common_cells/rr_arb_tree.sv]
// "assert (NumIn)" uses a 32-bit parameter as a boolean; upstream style.
lint_off -rule WIDTHTRUNC -file "*/common_cells*/src/rr_arb_tree.sv"
// "(i > rr_q)" genvar comparison constant under this parameterization.
lint_off -rule UNSIGNED   -file "*/common_cells*/src/rr_arb_tree.sv"

// [upstream dependency: axi/axi_pkg.sv]
// Width-extending arithmetic in beat-address helper functions; upstream
// constant math, not reachable from the router datapath.
lint_off -rule WIDTHEXPAND -file "*/axi-*/src/axi_pkg.sv"

// [core FlooNoC DUT RTL: floo_router.sv]
// NoLoopback assertion compares 1-bit hdr.collective_op against the 4-bit
// Unicast enum literal (0). Zero-extension makes the comparison correct.
lint_off -rule WIDTHEXPAND -file "*/floonoc/hw/floo_router.sv"

// [core FlooNoC DUT RTL: floo_output_arbiter.sv]
// "i < NumParallelRedRoutes" is constant-false with reductions disabled
// (NumParallelRedRoutes == 0); loop body correctly unreachable.
lint_off -rule UNSIGNED -file "*/floonoc/hw/floo_output_arbiter.sv"

// [UVM 1800.2-2017 library]
// The UVM base-class library is not Verilator-lint-clean; it is a pinned,
// unmodified third-party dependency. Scoped to the UVM source tree only.
lint_off -file "*/uvm*/src/*"

// [UVM macro expansions inside local TB code]
// `uvm_info/`uvm_error expand to "if (uvm_report_enabled(...))" where the
// function returns int; and randomize() returns int used in boolean
// context. Both are UVM API signatures, not local bugs. Matched narrowly
// on the message content so genuine width bugs in TB code still surface.
lint_off -rule WIDTHTRUNC -file "*tb/*" -match "*uvm_report_enabled*"
lint_off -rule WIDTHTRUNC -file "*tb/*" -match "*METHODCALL 'randomize'*"

// [core FlooNoC DUT RTL: floo_router.sv — UNDRIVEN, mesh lint only]
// `past_handshakes_d` DOES have a driver in floo_router.sv (the assign at
// its `gen_multicast` generate branch) — it is parameterization-dependent,
// not dead code: this bench's `EnMultiCast=0` elaborates `gen_unicast`
// instead, so that driver is elaborated away, while the `` `FF `` flop for
// `past_handshakes_q` sits outside the generate and always exists. Upstream
// itself flags the layout with a `// TODO (lleone): Move the folloiwng FF
// inside the multicast` comment right above it. Only surfaces under
// `-Wwarn-UNDRIVEN` (make lint-mesh); the single-router `lint` target does
// not enable this rule, so this entry is inert there.
//
// `-match` is pinned to the warning's MESSAGE BODY ("Signal is not driven:
// '<name>'"), not just the variable name, because Verilator's `-match`
// matches against the full formatted warning block INCLUDING the echoed
// source line — and the declaration `past_handshakes_q, past_handshakes_d`
// is one line, so a pattern on the bare name (e.g. `*past_handshakes_q*`)
// would suppress this warning too, and would keep suppressing an UNDRIVEN
// on EITHER signal even if the other one lost its driver. Pinning to
// `*not driven: 'past_handshakes_d'*` means the pattern only matches a
// warning whose message body names this exact signal — verified directly:
// swapping in `*not driven: 'past_handshakes_q'*` does NOT suppress this
// warning (`make lint-mesh` fails with it), even though both names sit on
// the same echoed source line.
//
// W7/W8 above share this same over-broad property (their `-match` patterns
// are also visible on an echoed source line, not just in the message body)
// but are single-router-only waivers, out of scope for this fix — not
// changed here.
lint_off -rule UNDRIVEN -file "*/floonoc/hw/floo_router.sv" -match "*not driven: 'past_handshakes_d'*"
